{"reply":"In **Chapter 26**, the boys are the ones who make the promise to study seem postponable: they invite Pinocchio to the seashore to see “A Shark as big as a mountain,” and when he says he must go to school, they answer, “You can go there tomorrow.” They then make the outing feel urgent by insisting the Shark may leave before he arrives. ([Chapter 26](#))

So the promise disappears through a quick shift in framing: studying becomes an ordinary obligation that can be delayed, while the outing becomes a rare opportunity that must happen now. The chapter also explicitly connects Pinocchio’s vulnerability to his companions, recalling warnings that “Those bad companions will sooner or later make you lose your love for study.” ([Chapter 26](#))

That may be why the scene feels uncomfortably familiar without implying that your evenings are simply the same as Pinocchio’s: a future intention can remain sincere and still lose to whatever feels immediate, social, or rewarding in the moment. When your own plan to study vanishes, what usually supplies the stronger “right now”—a particular activity, a tiredness, or the thought that tomorrow will be easier?","evidence_uses":[{"source_kind":"book_corpus","evidence_id":"pg500-v6bdc1734-ch26-ln3252-3308","source_location":"Chapter 26 — Pinocchio goes to the seashore with his friends to see the Terrible Shark., source lines 3252-3308","exact_quote":"“A Shark as big as a mountain”","supported_claims":["In **Chapter 26**, the boys are the ones who make the promise to study seem postponable: they invite Pinocchio to the seashore to see “A Shark as big as a mountain,” and when he says he must go to school, they answer, “You can go there tomorrow.”","They then make the outing feel urgent by insisting the Shark may leave before he arrives.","The chapter also explicitly connects Pinocchio’s vulnerability to his companions, recalling warnings that “Those bad companions will sooner or later make you lose your love for study.”"]}],"memory":{"kind":"no_memory_candidate","reason_code":"automatic_capture_disabled"}}

